<title>INDIA: India Balarampur Chini 1996/97 net up.</title>
<headline>India Balarampur Chini 1996/97 net up.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	    2.36	vs	1.95</p>
<p>    Net sales	 2,308.4	 vs  1,798.7</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)   *14.85	vs     26.02</p>
<p>    Other income	 40.4	 vs     17.6</p>
<p>    Expenditure     1,774.5	 vs  1,433.3</p>
<p>    Interest	    207.4	 vs    106.4</p>
<p>    Gross profit	366.9	 vs    276.6</p>
<p>    Depreciation	 90.4	 vs     56.5</p>
<p>    Tax		    35.0	  vs     nil</p>
<p>Note: *Sugar firm Balarampur Chini Mills said its earning per share dropped due to an enlarged equity capital of 187.6 million rupees against 75.0 million last year.</p>
<p>The company said the dividend would be decided in the next board meeting. It did not set a date for the board meeting. The firm said its loss on investment was 5.5 million rupees in 1996/97 from 24.8 million last year. The results are unaudited.</p>
<p>-- Bombay equities desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
